1
00:00:00,833 --> 00:00:01,767
<i>What's happening?
Are you okay?</i>

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,267
<i>Don't leave that spot,
it's dangerous.</i>

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,367
<i>My hunch was right,
we've been detected, Major!</i>

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:06,567
<i> Tomas Limjoco!</i>

5
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:07,667
<i> Surrender now!</i>

6
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,933
<i> How dare you betray me?</i>

7
00:00:10,067 --> 00:00:12,667
<i> You betrayed me, Tomas!</i>

8
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,000
<i>Do you really want
to go against me?</i>

9
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:15,667
<i>Major, my family
is in danger inside.</i>

10
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,300
<i> Stop your cruelty!</i>

11
00:00:17,433 --> 00:00:18,867
<i>[GUN FIRING]
Mom!</i>

12
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,900
<i> Relax, Brotherinlaw.</i>

13
00:00:20,033 --> 00:00:20,967
<i> Your family is still alive...</i>

14
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:21,700
<i> for now.</i>

15
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,933
<i> You animal!</i>

16
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:26,600
<i>If I hear even a hint of noise
or anyone disobeys,</i>

17
00:00:26,733 --> 00:00:28,200
<i> someone here will die.</i>

18
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:30,133
<i>Hello, Jin Ho?
Don't tell anyone that</i>

19
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:31,233
<i> I'm the one you're talking to.</i>

20
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:33,667
<i>This is the only way to save
your family.</i>

21
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,833
<i> We have to take the risk.</i>

22
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,533
<i>Major, I think it's time
we execute plan B.</i>

23
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,333
<i>Peter, Andrew said
we should start.</i>

24
00:00:40,467 --> 00:00:42,467
<i> Berdugo, your request is here.</i>

25
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,033
<i>We can't get them
all out at once</i>

26
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:45,033
<i> without being noticed.</i>

27
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:46,767
<i> Release your hostages.</i>

28
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:47,800
<i> Easy.</i>

29
00:00:47,933 --> 00:00:49,867
<i> We'll get there, Major.</i>

30
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:54,800
<i> [OBB]</i>

31
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,233
<i>Anyway, enough of this
interview.</i>

32
00:01:11,367 --> 00:01:12,733
<i> Major, thank you.</i>

33
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:14,267
You're easy to talk to.
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,767
You're going to save
a lot of lives.

35
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,433
<i> But isn't it poetic?</i>

36
00:01:17,567 --> 00:01:21,233
<i>That I gave you a medal
for being my valiant savior?</i>

37
00:01:21,367 --> 00:01:23,900
[APPLAUDING]

38
00:01:24,033 --> 00:01:25,467
<i> That's trash to me!</i>

39
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:28,267
I regret saving you.

40
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:29,367
<i> You talk too much!</i>

41
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:30,267
<i> Let's end this!</i>

42
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,433
Keep your word!

43
00:01:32,567 --> 00:01:33,833
Wait, wait!

44
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,433
How can we be sure
you won't harm my family?

45
00:01:38,567 --> 00:01:40,867
Looks like you've got serious
trust issues, Andrew.

46
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:44,667
<i>Let's just say control
is no longer in your hands.</i>

47
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,867
You just have to watch and wait.

48
00:01:48,467 --> 00:01:50,700
[PHONE BEEPING]

49
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:52,633
Joey, Jin Ho,
Berdugo is coming back!

50
00:01:52,767 --> 00:01:53,800
Joey?

51
00:01:53,933 --> 00:01:55,500
Where are you?

52
00:01:58,467 --> 00:01:59,467
[RATTLING IN DISTANCE]

53
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:00,800
Hey!

54
00:02:00,933 --> 00:02:03,133
- [SOBBING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:05,233
Mom! Mom!

56
00:02:05,367 --> 00:02:07,967
[CLAMORING]

57
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,567
- Mom! Mom!
- You move first!

58
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:10,833
- Move! Move! Go!
- Grandmother!

59
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:13,033
Joey, move first!
Go! Go!

60
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:14,967
[THUDDING]

61
00:02:16,033 --> 00:02:17,533
Go after them!

62
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,333
[GUN FIRING]

63
00:02:19,467 --> 00:02:20,533
Let's go!

64
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:21,467
What's that?

65
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,900
Hey!

66
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:27,233
[GRUNTING]
My child!

67
00:02:28,133 --> 00:02:29,233
Run! Hurry up!

68
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:31,033
- Let's go!
- My child!

69
00:02:31,267 --> 00:02:32,433
[SOBBING]

70
00:02:32,567 --> 00:02:33,533
Cruz, look!

71
00:02:33,667 --> 00:02:34,600
Copy, Sir!

72
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:36,700
Move! Move! Move!

73
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:40,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:02:40,833 --> 00:02:43,167
[KISSES BAWLING]

75
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,400
[CRUZ SHOUTS INDISTINCTLY]
<i> Unit 4, cover!</i>

76
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:46,467
[KISSES BAWLING]

77
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:02:52,633 --> 00:02:54,833
Jin Ho is still inside!

79
00:02:54,967 --> 00:02:55,900
We'll handle it!

80
00:02:56,033 --> 00:02:57,133
Get them out of the compound!

81
00:02:57,267 --> 00:02:59,967
- Yes, Sir!
- You animal! You animal!

82
00:03:00,867 --> 00:03:02,100
Let me go!

83
00:03:02,233 --> 00:03:04,000
- Come here...
- Let me go...

84
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:10,133
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

85
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:12,800
Mister, come on, let's go!
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:03:12,933 --> 00:03:14,767
Mister, please hurry up!

87
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:17,133
I need to go back
for my mommy, please!

88
00:03:17,267 --> 00:03:19,933
Mommy, don't leave us.

89
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:21,833
I'm coming with you.

90
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,667
I'm scared!

91
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:24,967
[WHIMPERING]

92
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:28,633
You have to be brave
for mommy and grandmother, okay?

93
00:03:28,767 --> 00:03:29,833
[BAWLING]

94
00:03:29,967 --> 00:03:32,067
We just need to find you
a safe place.

95
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,367
You'll be okay, I promise.

96
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:36,167
Harris, Harris...

97
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:38,600
Harris, take care
of your sister, okay?

98
00:03:38,733 --> 00:03:40,333
Take care of Kisses.

99
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:42,400
Go now, hurry!

100
00:03:42,533 --> 00:03:44,300
[KISSES BAWLING]

101
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:46,300
Go, go, Dear.

102
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:47,033
Hey!

103
00:03:47,167 --> 00:03:51,400
- [THUDDING]
- [GROANING]

104
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:53,767
We need to go back for my mommy.

105
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,467
I'll go with you.

106
00:03:55,633 --> 00:03:56,933
[CRUZ SHOUTS INDISTINCTLY]

107
00:03:57,067 --> 00:03:58,000
Move!

108
00:03:58,133 --> 00:03:59,367
Let's go!

109
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:03,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

110
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:13,933
- Andrew.
- Yvette.

111
00:04:14,067 --> 00:04:16,233
Joey, what are you doing here?

112
00:04:16,367 --> 00:04:17,800
[STAMMERS]
Go!

113
00:04:17,933 --> 00:04:19,167
Fire your guns!

114
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,200
I'll blow her brains out!

115
00:04:21,333 --> 00:04:23,033
Mom!
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

116
00:04:23,167 --> 00:04:24,767
No one fires!

117
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,867
You are an animal, Berdugo!

118
00:04:32,867 --> 00:04:33,600
[GUN FIRES]

119
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:34,733
Mom!

120
00:04:34,867 --> 00:04:36,600
[GUN FIRING]

121
00:04:36,733 --> 00:04:41,133
[HEAVY MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,500
[GUN FIRING]

123
00:04:43,633 --> 00:04:44,667
[TIRES SCREECH]

124
00:04:48,367 --> 00:04:50,700
Mom!

125
00:04:50,833 --> 00:04:54,500
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

126
00:04:56,300 --> 00:05:00,367
[GUNS FIRING]

127
00:05:04,033 --> 00:05:05,933
[GUNS FIRING]

128
00:05:06,067 --> 00:05:09,767
- [GUN FIRING]
- [MEN GROANING]

129
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:13,800
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

130
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:21,267
[GUNS FIRING]

131
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:25,400
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

132
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:28,767
[GUNS FIRING]

133
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:32,700
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

134
00:05:47,467 --> 00:05:49,333
- Mom!
- Mom!

135
00:05:49,467 --> 00:05:51,433
- Mom...
- Mom!

136
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:54,600
Mom...

137
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,900
Cruz, call an ambulance.

138
00:05:57,967 --> 00:05:59,200
<i> That animal Berdugo!</i>

139
00:05:59,333 --> 00:06:00,733
I should've been there!

140
00:06:01,167 --> 00:06:04,000
What chance do you have
against bullets, Peter?

141
00:06:04,133 --> 00:06:07,067
We're more useful here,
so let's keep going, okay?

142
00:06:08,233 --> 00:06:09,833
Okay, okay, okay.

143
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:11,933
There's so much going on!

144
00:06:14,167 --> 00:06:15,133
Mom!

145
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:17,033
Mommy...

146
00:06:19,767 --> 00:06:21,267
Mom...

147
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:23,600
Mom...

148
00:06:23,733 --> 00:06:25,067
Mom, I'm sorry.

149
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:27,167
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

150
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:28,533
I'm really sorry, Mom.

151
00:06:28,667 --> 00:06:29,867
I failed you again.

152
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,133
No...

153
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,233
You...

154
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:42,533
You never failed me, Son.

155
00:06:44,367 --> 00:06:46,933
Everything that happened...

156
00:06:48,267 --> 00:06:49,700
was my fault.

157
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:51,600
No.

158
00:06:51,733 --> 00:06:53,033
I'm sorry.

159
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:54,167
Mom, no.

160
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:55,400
Yvette...

161
00:06:55,533 --> 00:06:56,967
Mom...

162
00:06:58,033 --> 00:06:59,367
I'm sorry.

163
00:07:00,033 --> 00:07:02,033
I let you marry that...

164
00:07:02,167 --> 00:07:04,033
That monster.

165
00:07:04,167 --> 00:07:08,467
[SOBBING]

166
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,367
I wrote a letter,

167
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,033
it's under my bed.

168
00:07:12,167 --> 00:07:15,233
Get it, get it.

169
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,600
I'm sorry, my children.

170
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:21,100
- Mom! No...
- Mom!

171
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:22,700
I love you both.

172
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:25,567
I'm sorry.

173
00:07:26,167 --> 00:07:28,167
I'm sorry.

174
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:30,700
I'm sorry.

175
00:07:34,867 --> 00:07:38,067
[WHIMPERS]

176
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,333
- Mom! Mom!
- Mom! Mom!

177
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,967
- Mom!
- Mom?

178
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:47,400
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

179
00:07:52,233 --> 00:07:53,867
Mom!

180
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:57,100
[BAWLING]

181
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:03,100
[SOBBING]

182
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:07,200
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES♪]

183
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:16,500
Proceed to the hangar.

184
00:08:16,633 --> 00:08:17,833
Okay, Boss.

185
00:08:17,967 --> 00:08:20,000
The pilot is on the way,
Berdugo.

186
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,533
Good.

187
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:25,800
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:36,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:38,467
<i> Tirada</i> viewers...

190
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:41,833
Did you see how ruthless
Berdugo is?

191
00:08:42,667 --> 00:08:44,633
I need your help.

192
00:08:45,667 --> 00:08:48,233
If anyone sees Berdugo,

193
00:08:48,367 --> 00:08:50,533
report him to us and the police.

194
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,800
That shameless Berdugo
should not escape.

195
00:08:54,967 --> 00:08:56,967
He will pay for all of this.

196
00:08:57,100 --> 00:09:02,433
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

197
00:09:06,033 --> 00:09:07,367
The comments are coming so fast!

198
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,433
[WHIMPERS PLAYFULLY]

199
00:09:08,567 --> 00:09:09,700
I can't keep up.

200
00:09:09,833 --> 00:09:10,833
There, there.

201
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:14,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

202
00:09:15,467 --> 00:09:17,000
[PHONE CHIMES]

203
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,100
Oh, my god, Peter.

204
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:24,367
Look!

205
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,367
Berdugo's getaway vehicle!

206
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:30,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

207
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:32,133
<i> Guys, help us.</i>

208
00:09:32,267 --> 00:09:34,733
<i>Send this to the police
or Tirada Express.</i>

209
00:09:34,867 --> 00:09:37,167
<i>Berdugo's car is right
in front of me.</i>

210
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:39,533
There are only
a few viewers so far,

211
00:09:39,667 --> 00:09:40,733
so, the police need to see this.

212
00:09:40,867 --> 00:09:41,700
Wait.

213
00:09:41,833 --> 00:09:43,133
There.

214
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:46,333
That's it!

215
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:49,500
There! I told you,
you could help here!

216
00:09:50,733 --> 00:09:52,300
[SPEAKS IN VISAYAN LANGUAGE]

217
00:09:54,833 --> 00:09:56,400
<i>We're here now
at Dimapilis Street</i>

218
00:09:56,533 --> 00:09:58,733
<i>near the boundary of Alicia
and Tirona.</i>

219
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:01,600
<i>They've crossed Magano Highway.</i>

220
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:03,267
<i> Hurry.</i>

221
00:10:04,333 --> 00:10:05,933
What's that? A live broadcast?

222
00:10:06,067 --> 00:10:07,300
Yes, Dad.

223
00:10:07,433 --> 00:10:09,800
Peter and Elai connected
Andrew's live feed

224
00:10:09,933 --> 00:10:12,067
to the man following Berdugo.

225
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,100
We're going after Berdugo.

226
00:10:15,233 --> 00:10:17,633
Yvette, the ambulance
is on its way.

227
00:10:17,767 --> 00:10:19,233
Men, let's move!

228
00:10:19,367 --> 00:10:23,667
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,800
Andrew...

230
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,300
I know you want to go.

231
00:10:29,667 --> 00:10:31,600
I'll take care of mommy.

232
00:10:32,867 --> 00:10:35,400
Let's fulfill what she wanted.

233
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:38,400
Get Berdugo.

234
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:42,500
He will pay
for what he did to us.

235
00:10:42,633 --> 00:10:45,967
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:57,267
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,133
I know this is dangerous,
but it's exciting!

238
00:11:13,267 --> 00:11:14,533
All the viewers are on our side!

239
00:11:14,667 --> 00:11:15,567
[CHUCKLES]

240
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:17,400
This is it,
this is what I mean!

241
00:11:17,533 --> 00:11:18,600
This is what social media can do

242
00:11:18,733 --> 00:11:21,100
when you use it for good.
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

243
00:11:21,233 --> 00:11:22,267
That, that!

244
00:11:23,567 --> 00:11:26,867
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:31,967
Do you hear us?

246
00:11:32,433 --> 00:11:33,633
If you hear us,

247
00:11:33,767 --> 00:11:36,467
tell us immediately
where Berdugo is.

248
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:38,933
<i> We're now at Tirano Boulevard.</i>

249
00:11:39,067 --> 00:11:40,000
Okay, we're heading there.

250
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:44,100
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:11:55,767 --> 00:11:57,400
Is the plane ready?

252
00:11:57,533 --> 00:11:59,467
It's ready, Berdugo.

253
00:12:03,567 --> 00:12:05,233
[PHONE CHIMES]

254
00:12:05,367 --> 00:12:06,833
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:12:06,967 --> 00:12:09,367
Boss, Ambo sent something.

256
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:12,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

257
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,967
Boss, you were streamed live
during the hostage situation.

258
00:12:15,133 --> 00:12:16,700
Hundreds of thousands
were watching.

259
00:12:16,833 --> 00:12:18,333
Everyone saw your face
on social media.

260
00:12:18,467 --> 00:12:19,500
They know who you are...

261
00:12:19,633 --> 00:12:21,200
Shut up!

262
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:23,367
Looks like they'll never
leave me alone.

263
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:27,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

264
00:12:30,767 --> 00:12:32,200
[PHONE CHIMES]

265
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:34,633
Boss, we're live online again.

266
00:12:34,767 --> 00:12:36,500
Someone's chasing us.

267
00:12:36,633 --> 00:12:40,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,300
Slow down. Pull over.

269
00:12:49,467 --> 00:12:51,867
If they're still filming,
shoot them.

270
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:56,000
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,733
<i> Oh no, they noticed me.</i>

272
00:13:03,867 --> 00:13:04,933
<i> They might shoot me.</i>

273
00:13:05,067 --> 00:13:07,367
<i>Goodbye and good luck to you,
Boss Idol.</i>

274
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:08,933
What happened to him?

275
00:13:09,767 --> 00:13:10,733
Did he disappear?

276
00:13:10,867 --> 00:13:12,167
The live feed is gone.

277
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,767
It's gone.

278
00:13:13,900 --> 00:13:16,000
Maybe he lost his signal,

279
00:13:16,133 --> 00:13:17,800
or something stopped him.

280
00:13:17,933 --> 00:13:21,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:13:23,567 --> 00:13:28,367
Make a u-turn.

282
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:30,967
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

283
00:13:36,767 --> 00:13:37,967
<i> Okay, copy.</i>

284
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,767
See you at the first rest area.

285
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:42,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

286
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,867
Joey, the bus is here.

287
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,333
Right?

288
00:13:45,467 --> 00:13:48,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

289
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:57,433
<i> What's your plan?</i>

290
00:13:57,567 --> 00:14:00,033
We can still have Elai
for the livestream.

291
00:14:00,467 --> 00:14:01,600
Jin Ho, can you help us cover?

292
00:14:01,733 --> 00:14:02,800
Okay.

293
00:14:02,933 --> 00:14:04,233
What's my task?

294
00:14:04,367 --> 00:14:07,500
Joey, you'll talk to them
to help us trap Berdugo.

295
00:14:07,633 --> 00:14:09,000
But I'm not you.

296
00:14:09,133 --> 00:14:10,100
They don't know me.

297
00:14:10,233 --> 00:14:11,100
Can I do that?

298
00:14:11,233 --> 00:14:12,400
Yes!

299
00:14:12,533 --> 00:14:13,800
Go, Joey.

300
00:14:16,467 --> 00:14:17,767
Joey...

301
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:24,167
convince them to help us,
please.

302
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:25,633
I trust you.

303
00:14:25,767 --> 00:14:27,233
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:14:27,367 --> 00:14:28,833
Let's go, guys.

305
00:14:31,333 --> 00:14:32,633
Boss, you handle the pickup.

306
00:14:32,767 --> 00:14:34,433
- Okay, I'll drive.
- Okay, Sir.

307
00:14:34,567 --> 00:14:37,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

308
00:14:44,433 --> 00:14:46,333
Guys, ready?

309
00:14:46,467 --> 00:14:47,933
Ready!

310
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:50,767
Hurry up!

311
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:55,000
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

312
00:15:17,133 --> 00:15:19,700
<i> Tirada</i> and<i> Saludo</i> viewers...

313
00:15:19,833 --> 00:15:21,500
I'm not Boss Idol,

314
00:15:22,033 --> 00:15:24,367
but we have only one mission...

315
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,300
and that is to capture Berdugo.

316
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:31,533
You will be our eyes
on the road.

317
00:15:31,667 --> 00:15:35,533
If you have leads or if you know
where Berdugo is,

318
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,600
send it to us immediately
or to the police.

319
00:15:37,733 --> 00:15:41,233
And you, Berdugo,
I know you're watching.

320
00:15:41,367 --> 00:15:42,300
You cannot escape.

321
00:15:42,433 --> 00:15:44,600
You will pay for everything
you've done.

322
00:15:47,567 --> 00:15:51,267
[BUS REVVING]

323
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,500
<i> Guys, let's make a brigade,</i>

324
00:15:53,633 --> 00:15:57,800
<i>Hashtag catch Berdugo
to help Boss Idol.</i>

325
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:02,833
I made a mistake.

326
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:06,300
I should have
killed you all earlier.

327
00:16:06,433 --> 00:16:08,133
Boss, what if someone tracks us

328
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,033
and learns we're heading
to the hangar?

329
00:16:10,167 --> 00:16:11,800
We might get cornered.

330
00:16:11,933 --> 00:16:13,200
Just drive!

331
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:14,700
Tell the pilot

332
00:16:14,833 --> 00:16:17,533
to prepare the plane
at the airfield.

333
00:16:17,667 --> 00:16:19,033
Yes, Boss.

334
00:16:19,167 --> 00:16:23,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

335
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:27,400
Joey, where are we going now?

336
00:16:27,533 --> 00:16:29,333
What did the netizens say?

337
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:34,367
Peter, what's the update?

338
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,567
Here, here,
Elai and I are checking.

339
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:37,667
Here, here, some are coming in.

340
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,200
Wait, wait.

341
00:16:39,767 --> 00:16:41,467
There, checking...

342
00:16:42,767 --> 00:16:45,833
<i> Berdugo is at Francia Street.</i>

343
00:16:48,867 --> 00:16:51,500
<i>He passed Blanco Avenue
in Roxas City.</i>

344
00:16:51,633 --> 00:16:52,867
Roxas?

345
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:54,400
Roxas City? Is this it?

346
00:16:55,167 --> 00:16:56,900
He's misleading us!

347
00:16:57,033 --> 00:16:58,133
Joey, false alarm.

348
00:16:58,267 --> 00:16:59,500
It's just a prank.

349
00:16:59,633 --> 00:17:00,700
There are so many, wait!

350
00:17:00,833 --> 00:17:03,633
How do we know
which one is legit?

351
00:17:03,767 --> 00:17:05,267
This is no joke.

352
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,833
[BUS REVVING]

353
00:17:07,967 --> 00:17:09,133
<i> This is driving me crazy.</i>

354
00:17:09,267 --> 00:17:14,067
<i>No, it can't be.
That Berdugo cannot get away.</i>

355
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,300
<i>Catch him and make him pay
for what he did</i>

356
00:17:16,467 --> 00:17:18,633
<i> to Rebecca Dizon.</i>

357
00:17:18,767 --> 00:17:20,467
Thank you!

358
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:22,633
We need Berdugo's realtime
location

359
00:17:22,767 --> 00:17:24,267
before he escapes.

360
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:26,967
Relying on social media
to catch me?

361
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:29,867
Pathetic.

362
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,800
Berdugo, we're almost there.

363
00:17:32,933 --> 00:17:34,267
Good.

364
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:37,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

365
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:40,000
What? Still nothing?

366
00:17:40,667 --> 00:17:41,933
Nothing.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

367
00:17:42,067 --> 00:17:45,367
They're sending more videos,
but wrong car.

368
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,167
But they're persistent.
They want to help.

369
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:50,467
They're asking for details
about the car.

370
00:17:50,633 --> 00:17:52,100
[PHONE CHIMES]

371
00:17:53,667 --> 00:17:55,567
Wait, wait,
we have something new.

372
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:58,900
[BUS REVVING]

373
00:17:59,033 --> 00:18:03,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

374
00:18:03,733 --> 00:18:05,567
<i>Looks like Berdugo is heading
to the airfield.</i>

375
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:08,500
<i>Inform the police and Boss Idol
immediately.</i>

376
00:18:08,633 --> 00:18:09,800
Wait, I'll put this
on<i> Tirada</i> live,

377
00:18:09,933 --> 00:18:10,867
right next to Joey.

378
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,367
Wait, wait.

379
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:13,867
Peter, don't!

380
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,300
What?

381
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:26,833
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

382
00:18:34,767 --> 00:18:35,833
Why?

383
00:18:35,967 --> 00:18:38,000
I just thought, there were only
8 viewers that time.

384
00:18:38,133 --> 00:18:39,833
It wasn't on Berdugo's
radar yet.

385
00:18:39,967 --> 00:18:41,100
But if he sees it,

386
00:18:41,233 --> 00:18:43,567
he could block it
like he did earlier.

387
00:18:49,233 --> 00:18:50,833
I agree.

388
00:18:50,967 --> 00:18:52,967
We should gatekeep
this information.

389
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:56,367
Let's inform Andrew first,
then to Major Delgado.

390
00:18:56,533 --> 00:19:00,667
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

391
00:19:04,533 --> 00:19:06,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

392
00:19:06,633 --> 00:19:08,400
What the hell are they up to?

393
00:19:12,233 --> 00:19:13,367
Turn right there.

394
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:15,667
There's a shortcut
to the hangar.

395
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:20,300
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

396
00:19:20,433 --> 00:19:22,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

397
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:31,567
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

398
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:19:45,733 --> 00:19:48,400
[PHONE RINGING]

400
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:53,400
Mr. Co, why are you calling?

401
00:19:53,533 --> 00:19:56,067
<i>What's this all over
social media?</i>

402
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,700
<i> You're exposed, Tomas.</i>

403
00:19:57,833 --> 00:20:00,733
<i>How can we still trust
doing business with you?</i>

404
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:03,300
This is just a minor setback,
Martin.

405
00:20:03,467 --> 00:20:06,400
I'm on my way
to my new business location.

406
00:20:06,533 --> 00:20:08,700
I'll update you
when I get there.

407
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:09,867
<i> Fix this...</i>

408
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,633
<i> or I'll convince
the entire network to pull out.</i>

409
00:20:12,767 --> 00:20:14,533
You know you can't do that.

410
00:20:14,667 --> 00:20:17,333
Unless you want
your family to know

411
00:20:17,467 --> 00:20:20,100
what you're really doing?

412
00:20:20,233 --> 00:20:22,067
<i> Are you blackmailing me?</i>

413
00:20:23,067 --> 00:20:25,767
I'm just doing business.

414
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:27,600
Let's talk again later.

415
00:20:30,833 --> 00:20:32,433
I thought we were already close?

416
00:20:32,567 --> 00:20:34,133
Five minutes, Berdugo.

417
00:20:34,267 --> 00:20:36,300
Make it one, damn it!

418
00:20:36,467 --> 00:20:40,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

419
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,833
[PHONE RINGING]

420
00:20:44,967 --> 00:20:46,833
Hello? Joey?

421
00:20:46,967 --> 00:20:47,767
<i> Hello, Dad?</i>

422
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:49,167
According to the rider,

423
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:52,367
Berdugo entered
Santan Woods Subdivision,

424
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:55,100
it's the alternate route
to the airfields.

425
00:20:55,233 --> 00:20:56,433
Copy.

426
00:20:56,833 --> 00:20:58,367
Okay.

427
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:02,067
All units, please proceed
to Santan Woods Subdivision!

428
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:06,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

429
00:21:09,633 --> 00:21:13,667
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

430
00:21:16,533 --> 00:21:17,467
Let's split up!

431
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:18,567
Berdugo, there are police here!

432
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:19,767
Shoot them!

433
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:22,433
[GUN FIRING]

434
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:25,833
[GUN FIRING]

435
00:21:25,967 --> 00:21:27,700
[TIRES SCREECH]
